["https://spdx.org/rdf/3/terms/Core/ExternalIdentifierType/nli", "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment", "[Natural Location Identifier (NLI)](https://eccma.org/enli-eccma-natural-location-identifier/) is a 14- or 15-character alphanumeric string standardized by [ISO 8000-118](https://www.iso.org/standard/85428.html) that uniquely identifies a three-dimensional geographic point location. The identifier is generated from geodetic coordinates and elevation data. For electronic storage, the `ISO.NLI:` prefix shall be retained (e.g., `ISO.NLI:41TS8M-A8ELTQ-H2`).", "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString", "en", ""]
["_:Nc2bf447d5bb5428fad74632aa5160081", "http://www.w3.org/ns/shacl#class", "https://spdx.org/rdf/3/terms/Core/Agent", "globalId", "", ""]
["https://spdx.org/rdf/3/terms/Build/buildType", "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment", "A buildType is a hint that is used to indicate the toolchain, platform, or\ninfrastructure that the build was invoked on.", "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString", "en", ""]
["https://spdx.org/rdf/3/terms/Software/additionalPurpose", "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment", "Provides additional purpose information of the software artifact.", "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString", "en", ""]
["_:N05eb71905c4448ab92b2e9cc9ec480b0", "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type", "http://www.w3.org/ns/shacl#SPARQLConstraint", "globalId", "", ""]
["_:Nf293ccc621514665bad462f2eba1f24b", "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type", "http://www.w3.org/ns/shacl#SPARQLConstraint", "globalId", "", ""]
["https://spdx.org/rdf/3/terms/Core/ExternalIdentifierType/eori", "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment", "[Economic Operators Registration and Identification (EORI) number](https://taxation-customs.ec.europa.eu/customs/customs-procedures-import-and-export/customs-operations/economic-operators-registration-and-identification-number-eori_en) is a unique identifier for businesses undertaking customs operations across European Union customs territory, such as import, export, and transit. It consists of an ISO 3166-1 alpha-2 country code followed by a national identifier of up to 15 alphanumeric characters (e.g., `PL1234567890ABCDE`).", "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString", "en", ""]
["https://spdx.org/rdf/3/terms/Core/specVersion", "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type", "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#DatatypeProperty", "globalId", "", ""]
["https://spdx.org/rdf/3/terms/Operations/ExportControlClassification", "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type", "http://www.w3.org/ns/shacl#NodeShape", "globalId", "", ""]
["https://spdx.org/rdf/3/terms/Core/RequirementStatusType/draft", "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment", "A requirement is considered a draft state and may be modified before being submitted for review.", "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString", "en", ""]
